    "Early120–180 and final540+ used-heap minima differ by +4,182,068 bytes. This is a real difference in sampled counters and must not be hidden behind the fixed web-memory 10 MB reading.",
    "The same windows used-heap medians differ by only +665,016 bytes, while maxima differ by -63,456 bytes. Minimum-only comparisons are sensitive to sample/reclamation phase.",
    "Minutes7–10 used minima are 8,106,448 / 8,099,628 / 8,021,152 / 8,036,664 bytes, with medians 8,903,072 / 9,040,752 / 8,805,818 / 8,811,512 bytes. This is an observed late plateau, not continuing monotonic growth.",
    "Late total-heap capacity remains within 19,468,288–19,992,576 bytes; backing storage remains about 263–266 kB. Embedder samples fluctuate with repeated substantial decreases instead of accumulating monotonically.",
    "Negative adjacent sample deltas demonstrate naturally occurring decreases without forced GC. They are compatible with reclamation/allocation cycles but do not identify GC type, object retention causes, or prove absence of leaks."
